1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,762
She walked out of Carnegie's mansion... and dropped a $2,000,000 note he never signed.

2
00:00:05,012 --> 00:00:09,880
A man from Ohio saw it... and one day, an Ohio bank would collapse.

3
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:13,165
Her secret, she told him: she was Carnegie's daughter.

4
00:00:13,365 --> 00:00:17,900
Soon banks were lending to Carnegie's "daughter." Nobody asked Carnegie.

5
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:23,225
Some at 25%. By one estimate, about $2 million in all.

6
00:00:23,475 --> 00:00:26,077
She played the heiress on Cleveland's Euclid Avenue.

7
00:00:26,277 --> 00:00:29,316
Then one lender wanted his $190,000 back.

8
00:00:29,516 --> 00:00:34,119
Carnegie's office said: he didn't know her, and hadn't signed a note in over 30 years.

9
00:00:34,369 --> 00:00:38,573
In Oberlin, Ohio, depositors ran on their bank. It failed.

10
00:00:39,473 --> 00:00:41,116
She died in prison three years later.

11
00:00:41,466 --> 00:00:46,301
Carnegie never gave her a cent. The banks did... for his name.
